# Context management

## Scope

- Work one task at a time. Do not read or modify files outside the current task's scope.
- Ask before touching more than ~5 files or doing large refactors.

## Discovery

- Use codebase search and `docs/codebase-map.md` to locate code before opening files.
- Never read whole directories speculatively.
- Read only the `spec/` files relevant to the current task.

## Output

- Show diffs or changed sections only; never re-print unchanged files in full.

## Project memory

- After finishing a task that adds, moves, or renames classes or components, update `docs/codebase-map.md` (module → purpose → key files).
